# Report branding (DWES)

All generated reports must use the **central branding helpers** — never one-off headers.

## Source of truth

- `backend/src/common/report-branding.ts` — logo path, PDF header, Excel header
- Logo asset: `public/logo-full.png` and `backend/assets/report-logo.png`

## PDF reports

Use `drawPdfReportHeader(doc, { title, subtitle })` from `report-branding.ts`.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
let y = drawPdfReportHeader(doc, {
  title: 'Project Completion Report',
  subtitle: `Ingenious Network FZC · ${code}`,
});
doc.y = y;

// ❌ BAD — duplicate text-only header, no logo
doc.text('Digital Wiring Execution System', { align: 'center' });
```

Applies to: project PDF, frame wiring PDF, director PDF, any new PDF export.

## Excel reports

Use `prependExcelReportHeader(wb, ws, { title, subtitle, colCount })` for ExcelJS workbooks.

For new Excel exports, prefer **ExcelJS** over raw SheetJS so the logo can embed.

## On-screen preview

Report preview modals must show `CompanyLogo` in the header bar (`ReportPreviewModal`, `CompletionReport`).

## Do not

- Hardcode logo paths outside `report-branding.ts`
- Ship PDF/Excel without the company logo in the header band
- Remove `Ingenious Network FZC` / DWES subtitle when replacing headers
